# Trellis-client e2e (Playwright)

**Dev port:** `localhost:$TRELLIS_PORT` (default **1414**) — not 9292 (threlte-skeleton).

**Node:** use **22** (`nvm use` reads repo `.nvmrc`).

## Who runs Playwright

| Role | Playwright? |
|------|-------------|
| Executor | **No** — `pnpm check` only; hand off "ready for e2e" |
| QA / Reviewer | **Yes** — one serialized run via wrapper |
| Other tabs | **No** — do not invoke raw `playwright test` |

Only **one** Playwright runner at a time. The wrapper acquires `.agent/playwright.lock` (waits up to 10m, then exits **75** `PLAYWRIGHT_BUSY`).

## Dev server check

Dev is usually already running (`just run` / `jr`). **Never restart a healthy stack.**

```bash
curl -sf "http://localhost:${TRELLIS_PORT:-1414}/api/graph/health"
```

## Playwright (always use wrapper)

```bash
# Preferred — dev up on :1414; lock + chromium-only + workers=1
pnpm --filter @trellis/web test:e2e

# Scoped spec (from AC)
pnpm --filter @trellis/web test:e2e tests/e2e/navigation.spec.ts

# Full browser matrix (human / CI only)
PW_ALL_BROWSERS=1 pnpm --filter @trellis/web test:e2e:raw

# Cold start (slow — avoid in agent loops)
PW_COLD=1 pnpm --filter @trellis/web test:e2e

# Bypass lock (human debugging only)
pnpm --filter @trellis/web test:e2e:raw
```

Wrapper: `apps/web/scripts/test-e2e.mjs` · config: `apps/web/playwright.config.ts`

Missing browsers: `pnpm --filter @trellis/web exec playwright install chromium`

## Shell chrome invariant

**`AccountRailCluster`** mounts in **`AppHeader.vue`** only (header right, after `AppMenubar`). **Never** on `IconRail` end zone. E2E: `campus-dock-resident.spec.ts` asserts header placement.

## agent-browser pilot (exploratory QA)

Optional CLI for ad-hoc agent verification — **not** a Playwright replacement.

```bash
# One-shot pilot (dev on :1414)
./scripts/agent-browser-pilot.sh

# Manual session
export AGENT_BROWSER_SESSION=trellis-qa
agent-browser open "http://localhost:1414/workspace/browse?type=note&testAuthBypass=true"
agent-browser snapshot -i -c -d 4
agent-browser find role button click --name "Lobby notifications"
agent-browser screenshot .agent/qa.png
agent-browser close
```

Project config: `agent-browser.json` · MCP: `.mcp.json` → `agent-browser` server (`agent-browser mcp`).
